WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.468
-My first guest
is a talented actor

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.470
who stars in the new movie
"Wild Mountain Thyme,"

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.806
which is in theaters and
On Demand December 11th.

00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:09.809
Here is Jamie Dornan.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.645
Hey, bud!
Oh, it's good to see you, pal.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.882
-Good to see you, too, man.
-I know, crazy circumstances,

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.884
but how are you
and your family doing?

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:22.187
I know you have three daughters
under the age of 8, right?

00:00:22.187 --> 00:00:23.722
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:25.458
And you have two around
that same age, right?

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.426
-Yep. And what has
the past nine months

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:30.697
been like with three kids?

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:33.766
-I think it's kind of --
It's been all-encompassing.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:35.768
You know, it's kind of been
the agony and the ecstasy,

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:38.438
like, in the same
period of time.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:42.275
-Yeah, yeah.
-Some of the most

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.710
challenging days
I've ever had as a parent,

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.146
as we've ever had as parents.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:49.716
And then some of the most fun
to spend all this time together.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:50.884
You know, kids are amazing,

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.052
'cause they truly live
in the moment.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:55.888
So they're not concerned
about what's happening

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:59.292
and why the world
is the way it is at this age.

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:00.593
You know, they're just,

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.328
"This is what we have now.
Let's have fun."

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.764
So, like, that's a great thing
to be around, you know?

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.566
-I saw you took the plunge

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.802
and rejoined Instagram
in quarantine.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:11.070
Tell me about
your first post here.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:15.308
What is going on here?
What happened to you?

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:18.178
-I mean, it looks like
I'm the most committed

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.746
actor ever auditioning
for Blue Man Group.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:23.917
-[ Laughs ]
-I knew that was you!

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.552
I knew that was you.
You ignored me.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.921
I go, "Jamie, hello.
We have a thing,"

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:31.590
and you're just like
real quiet, and...

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.060
With your turtleneck,
and you walked off the stage.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.263
-[ Laughs ]
-What was happening there?

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:41.166
-What's actually happening is,
I had to get this

00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:44.637
full body cast -- or, upper body
cast and head cast made

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:47.373
for a job, which I was about
to start shooting

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.575
when the pandemic hit,
and actually,

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.044
I'm not able
to shoot that anymore

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.712
'cause of schedules,
so someone else

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.080
is now playing that character.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.883
'Cause that is a hellish
experience, doing that.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:02:00.018
I don't know if you've had that
done, but it's really,

00:02:00.018 --> 00:02:02.088
really uncomfortable,
and I'm not a panicky person,

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.789
but I had a full panic attack.

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:06.992
Because I'm not a great
nose breather anyway,

00:02:06.992 --> 00:02:09.228
but they put, like,
two little holes in your nose,

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:10.896
and that was the only way
I could breathe.

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:13.932
So, I was really struggling,
and it's like 45 minutes.

00:02:13.932 --> 00:02:16.368
But I've been told that
if I ever

00:02:16.368 --> 00:02:18.270
have to do it again
for anything,

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:22.975
I won't have to
'cause they have my cast now.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.378
So it's the only time
I ever have to do it in my life.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.781
-Yeah, it's currently
a mannequin at Macy's.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:32.285
It's in the front window.
Congratulations.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:35.621
-I'm delighted.
-I did that for "SNL,"

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:38.057
where they did the thing,
but it didn't take 45 minutes.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.992
They just -- I just did
a face thing, though, too.

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:42.695
But, actually, you know,
I have such a big Irish face

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:46.532
that it did take 45 minutes
and extra plaster.

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:47.766
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:47.766 --> 00:02:51.070
They go, "Gosh, you have
a really big head."

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.573
What else have you taken up
in quarantine?

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:58.945
Have you had time to focus on
any hobbies or any new talents?

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:02.148
-You know, like everybody,
I thought,

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:05.851
"How can I use this time
to the best of my ability

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:08.887
when I have so much of it?"
and I -- you know,

00:03:08.887 --> 00:03:15.328
I signed up for, like, a
fast-learning harmonica course.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:18.064
I -- You know,
it was one of those things,

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:20.733
it's on the side of your e-mail,
your inbox, and it's like,

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:23.436
"Learn harmonica -- in three
weeks, you'll be an expert."

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:27.340
And instead of $179,
it's like $46 or something,

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.376
so I was like, "Yeah, okay."
-That's a deal.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.944
-Haven't played once.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.346
-Oh, my God.
You didn't even do one lesson?

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:37.850
-In fact, I didn't even
open the trial, no.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:40.452
-[ Laughs ]
-No.

00:03:40.452 --> 00:03:41.721
But, look, I have it.
-You had the intention.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.489
Oh, you have
the harmonica there!

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.392
-Yeah.
-Oh, my good--

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:49.462
It's fairly simple. You could
probably figure it out.

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:53.533
♪♪

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.135
I think you should start
teaching the lessons.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.471
I know that song.
Of course.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:03:59.605
-Should I take that on the road,

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:01.440
like a one-man show,
like Dick Van Dyke?

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.877
-If you don't, I think you're
wasting a lot of -- yeah.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:08.013
That's a big opportunity there
that you should take.

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:11.617
I think, let's go back
to talking about your acting.

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:13.553
I was so excited
about this movie,

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.054
because I love
romantic comedies.

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.823
I'm Irish, I think Irelanders

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:19.392
are just so gorgeous
and beautiful.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.427
It's called
"Wild Mountain Thyme" --

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:26.865
T-H-Y-M-E,
and it was filmed in Ireland,

00:04:26.865 --> 00:04:28.968
set not too far
from where you grew up.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.870
Is that true?
-Yeah.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.506
I mean, it's based
on John Patrick Shanley,

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.374
who wrote directed our movie.

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:38.244
He did a play on Broadway called
"Outside Mullingar."

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.345
Mullingar is in County Meath,
which is --

00:04:40.345 --> 00:04:44.316
Yeah, I'm from County Down.
It's probably 200 miles

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:48.120
from where I grew up,
so not a million miles away.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.855
Yeah, and it's a strange story.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:51.990
I don't know if you're familiar
with Shanley's movies

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.327
and the way he writes,
but they're quite heightened,

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.028
fantastical kind of worlds.

00:04:56.028 --> 00:05:01.133
And this is almost like a fairy
tale, like a fable, you know?

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:04.236
It's very romantic,
but it's kind of otherworldly,

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:07.774
and Emily Blunt and I play these
two quite disconnected,

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:09.842
quite strange Irish farmers

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.245
who are sort of
destined to be together

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:14.680
but can't work out a way
to be together.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.916
But, yeah,
that's kind of it in a nutshell.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.884
-It's a great cast.

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:21.620
It's you, Emily Blunt
as your love interest.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.323
Jon Hamm, who is just a friend,

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:25.724
and just, gosh,
we love him here.

00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:28.761
Christopher Walken, who is --

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.330
Luckily, I got to work
with that guy,

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:35.467
I think, four times on "SNL,"
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:38.070
He plays your father.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:42.441
Isn't he the most fun,
interesting guy?

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:44.443
-Yeah.
But also, you know,

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.311
he's Christopher Walken.

00:05:46.311 --> 00:05:48.681
I mean, it literally
doesn't get more kind of

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.584
iconic, I don't think,
in our game.

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:54.052
-Yeah.
-He's, as you know well,

00:05:54.052 --> 00:05:56.856
he's actually just, like,
the sweetest guy in the world.

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:59.658
He's really -- and he's played
so many sinister characters

00:05:59.658 --> 00:06:03.062
and so many weighted, heavy,
sort of frightening characters,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.696
and he's, like,
the sweetest dude.

00:06:04.696 --> 00:06:09.802
He was, like, really,
just very connected and calm.

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:12.171
-He's a great dancer.
-Amazing.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:15.274
I mean, on top of acting,
he can do everything, yeah.

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:17.510
After you talked with him
for a while,

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:20.112
do you find yourself starting
to lean into the impression

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:21.814
a little bit
when you talk to him?

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:24.216
-Dude, I think it's, like,
the sort of --

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:26.852
You know, it's like
the equivalent of having

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:30.256
to sit on your hands
so that you don't start

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:33.792
to gesture him
or start to, like, mimic him.

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:36.529
I'm not a brilliant mimic.
You are.

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.330
I wouldn't say
I'm a great mimic,

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.299
but everyone
has a Christopher Walken.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:42.334
Like, everyone has one.

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:45.771
So you're sort of really
pushing yourself not to do it.

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:49.341
Because imagine how many times
people do it to him, you know?

00:06:49.341 --> 00:06:51.009
It's bad.
And, actually, I think

00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:53.545
you realize in person,
like, it's more --

00:06:53.545 --> 00:06:55.781
You know, the impressions just
become their own thing

00:06:55.781 --> 00:06:57.883
that they're way more
pushed than the reality.

00:06:57.883 --> 00:06:59.685
-Oh, yeah.
Yeah, exactly.

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.653
But, I mean, I find myself --
I do it all the time

00:07:01.653 --> 00:07:05.291
even just interviewing --
even you, I find myself

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:08.394
thinking I can do
a pretty good Irish accent.

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:10.596
-Yeah.
-My key to the Irish accent,

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.231
for me --
I would never attempt one --

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:14.800
but I just keep
saying the word "Em."

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.670
Em, em, em, em, em, em...

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:20.306
And that's all you keep saying.

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:23.475
-That can get you pretty far.
That can get you, like,

00:07:23.475 --> 00:07:24.810
a good night out in a pub.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.412
You can just get by
with just saying that.

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:28.514
-I should learn
how to play harmonica.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.416
I shouldn't even
think about acting.

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:33.586
But I heard Emily Blunt
introduced you

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:36.555
to something you call
"acting juice" on the set.

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:38.857
What's acting juice?

00:07:38.857 --> 00:07:42.428
-So, I actually don't even know
the brand name, and I should,

00:07:42.428 --> 00:07:43.996
because if I start
telling people,

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:46.265
then they'll send me a load
of it, and I'll be delighted.

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.901
-[ Laughs ]
-But she had just done

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:52.237
this movie, "Jungle Cruise,"
with Dwayne Johnson,

00:07:52.237 --> 00:07:56.174
and I guess when Johnson
got her on to this,

00:07:56.174 --> 00:08:01.580
it's like an energy drink,
and so she had loads of it

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.250
with her in Ireland.
Like, she'd had it shipped over.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.418
She's like,
"Do you want to try one?"

00:08:06.418 --> 00:08:07.987
And that was
just this fateful day

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:11.590
that I tried
this great-flavored juice.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.626
And it is like --
I don't know.

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:16.195
It's like Red Bull times 10

00:08:16.195 --> 00:08:18.063
but apparently
not as bad for you.

00:08:18.063 --> 00:08:21.100
And it just gives you --
Makes you feel like

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.934
you're kind of maybe
about to have a heart attack,

00:08:22.934 --> 00:08:26.706
what I imagine that feels like.
-That's the slogan.

00:08:26.706 --> 00:08:28.474
That's the slogan
for the energy drink.

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:30.142
-[ Laughing ]
-"If you drink this,

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:31.577
you'll feel like..."
-Unique selling point.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.379
-"...you might
have a heart attack," yeah.

00:08:33.379 --> 00:08:35.414
-You feel like
you're having a heart attack,

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:37.249
but you're okay, you won't.

00:08:37.249 --> 00:08:39.918
-Yeah, "Legally,
you can't sue us."

00:08:39.918 --> 00:08:41.454
-That sort of sustains
for a while.

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:44.423
But it just got to the point
where Emily and I

00:08:44.423 --> 00:08:46.291
convinced ourselves
that we sort of couldn't act

00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:49.595
without this stuff,
so we were just calling it

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:51.063
"acting juice"
and we'd be really panicking

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:53.332
if they were like,
"Okay. Guys, we're gonna shoot

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:54.866
in about five minutes.
You ready for that scene?"

00:08:54.866 --> 00:08:56.368
And we'd be like, "Yeah, yeah,"
and then be like...

00:08:56.368 --> 00:09:00.205
"Are we ready? There's no
acting juice anywhere!"

00:09:00.205 --> 00:09:01.940
-"I don't know
what to do anymore!

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.310
I need the acting juice!"

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.545
-Honestly, it was --
Luckily, I've done a movie since

00:09:06.545 --> 00:09:07.980
and I didn't have
any acting juice,

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.248
and it all went okay, so I don't
think I'm reliant on it.

00:09:10.248 --> 00:09:12.084
-Yeah, you still got the chops.

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:14.653
And, gosh, the chemistry
between you guys was perfect.

00:09:14.653 --> 00:09:17.123
So, whatever it was, it worked.

00:09:17.123 --> 00:09:19.525
I want to show a clip.
Here's Jamie Dornan

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:22.228
and Emily Blunt
in "Wild Mountain Thyme."

00:09:22.228 --> 00:09:23.429
Take a look.

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:25.197
-Anthony!

00:09:25.197 --> 00:09:26.599
Oh!

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:34.039
-[ Laughing ]

00:09:34.039 --> 00:09:35.340
Are you all right?

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.608
-I'm fine.

00:09:36.608 --> 00:09:38.377
-What are you doing out there?

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:40.979
-Fishing.
-That was fishing?

00:09:40.979 --> 00:09:43.782
-Yeah.
-Without your rod?

00:09:43.782 --> 00:09:45.985
Who were you talking to?
-Wasn't talking.

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:48.821
-Looked to be talking, then
swatting, then you jumped in.

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:51.089
-I did not.
It's the Kellys that jump in.

00:09:51.089 --> 00:09:52.625
I'm a Reilly.
-You're a Reilly.

00:09:52.625 --> 00:09:53.793
-What are you doing
down by the river?

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:55.494
-What I've been doing --
after this one.

00:09:55.494 --> 00:09:57.129
-Well, you're not still
from the night before?

00:09:57.129 --> 00:09:58.363
-I am.

00:09:58.363 --> 00:10:00.699
-Good God in haven,
you look the worst for it.

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:02.735
-Well, thanks so much.
You don't look perfect yourself.

